{
  "name": "Morning Brief – trending GitHub repos",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## ☀️ Morning Brief — trending GitHub repos\n**What:** every hour (or on demand via the webhook) find the most-starred **new** GitHub repos for a topic, enrich the breakout ones with their README and post one digest to Discord.\n\n**APIs:** GitHub Search API → GitHub README API → Discord webhook\n**Knobs:** all in **Config** (topic, lookback days, star threshold, top N)\n**Secrets:** only in n8n Credentials (Discord webhook URL, webhook token) — nothing hard-coded.\n\nWebhook test: `GET /webhook/morning-brief` + header `X-Webhook-Token`; `?topic=n8n` to change topic, `?simulate=github-down` to test the error path.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 580,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "5a6b7c8d-0001-4e5f-8a9b-000000000001",
      "name": "Note: overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -48,
        -416
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 🔀 IF: breakout ≥ 500 ⭐ in 7 days?\n**true →** fetch the README (1 extra API call) and show a rich card with a teaser.\n**false →** compact one-line entry, no extra call.\n\nWhy 500: the #1–#2 new `ai-agents` repos of a week sit around 600–1,100 ⭐, the rest of the top 5 around 200–470 — 500 separates \"breaking out\" from \"rising\" and keeps README calls (unauthenticated GitHub limit: 60/h) for the repos that matter.",
        "height": 230,
        "width": 480,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "5a6b7c8d-0002-4e5f-8a9b-000000000002",
      "name": "Note: routing",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1152,
        -416
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### ⚠️ Error handling — nothing fails silently\n1. **Retries:** every HTTP/Discord node retries (3 tries, 2–3 s apart) — covers blips and rate-limit hiccups.\n2. **GitHub search fails →** red *error output* → outage alert posted to Discord; the run ends as \"degraded\".\n3. **README fails →** *Continue on fail*: the repo stays in the digest marked \"README unavailable\".\n4. **Anything unexpected** (e.g. 0 repos, Discord down) → the workflow fails → the **Error Workflow** posts a 🚨 alert with the execution link.",
        "height": 175,
        "width": 720,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "5a6b7c8d-0003-4e5f-8a9b-000000000003",
      "name": "Note: errors",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        448,
        304
      ]
    },
    {
